antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  the results of immunohistochemical staining for progesterone receptor protein are for investigational use only  they must not be used for clinical purposes  added by  frederick carl koerner  m d  signed on  29 removed_month 94 at 15 03 gross description  two specimen parts are received fresh in the frozen section lab  each  labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name  unit number  and the following  labeled  right breast biopsy  is a removed_date x removed_date x 2 0cm  yellow  semifirm piece of fatty breast tissue with a removed_date x 0 3cm tan skin ellipse  and a localizing wire in place  the specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a 1 0cm in diameter  well defined  semifirm nodule adjacent to the hook of the wire and located 0 2cm from the deep inked margin  a representative section of this nodule is frozen as fx 1 and submitted in a  the remainder of the nodule is submitted in b d  the ends and body of the skin ellipse are submitted in e   f  respectively  the other tissue in g k  labeled  right axillary node  is a removed_date x removed_date x 1 5cm tan  semifirm lymph node  sectioned perpendicular to the long axis to reveal a tan  fleshy cut surface  no discrete lesions are noted  a representative section is frozen as fx 2  and saved frozen  half of the remaining tissue is fixed in formalin overnight  and now submitted in l o  the remainder of the tissue is submitted in p q  following b 5 fixation  a portion of tissue is kept for possible electron microscopy   tie   received fresh   labeled remove_patient_name  patient s name and unit number  are four more parts  these parts sat in an operating room refrigerator for two days before being sent to pathology  according to a notation on the requisition  labeled  right breast  fibroadenoma  frozen section diagnosis  2  axillary lymph node  metastatic anaplastic tumor cell  o r  resident  horace c  wu  md o r  diagnosis by  austin l  vickery  m d                                                                                  source care unit  mgh inpatient  flr unknown  reports to  barbara lynn smith  m d  alik farber  m d  mark atkinson vangorder  m d  part a  right breast biopsy part b  right axillary lymph node  biopsy for frozen part c  right axillary dissection part d  , Absent.
