accession number   removed_accession_id  report status  final type  surgical pathology pathology report   removed_accession_id  operation date  28 removed_month 97 accessioned on  28 removed_month 97 at 15 12 clinical data  left   excisional biopsy  invasive lobular carcinoma  present in five of five sections  representing three fragments   extending to the edges of the biopsy  note  no lymphatic or vascular invasion is identified  no in situ tumor is identified  because the biopsy is received as three fragments  the actual size and status of margins cannot be assessed  the tumor diameters on the two largest fragments are 0 9cm and 1 3cm  respectively  measured from slides  diagnosis by  john h  eichhorn  m d  signed on  30 removed_month 97 at 12 47                                                                                     receptor immunohistochemistry addendum     results of staining of fixed tissue for hormone receptor proteins breast  left   the tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  the tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  see note  note  in this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  when we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   in this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesteron